From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2000
From: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btrtl: propagate register-read error instead of swallowing it

drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c: in the RTL firmware probe path, an
unconditional return after a register read silently masked
negative register-read errors.  Return the actual error so bluetooth
core can surface the failure to userspace and the firmware load can
be retried rather than wedging the controller on a half-loaded
firmware.

Ported from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds:
  80015-bluetooth-btrtl-return-register-read-error.patch

Signed-off-by: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
[ported: applied verbatim from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds
  80015-bluetooth-btrtl-return-register-read-error.patch]
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c
index 7f54d2d2d..929874535 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c
@@ -1074,7 +1074,6 @@ struct btrtl_device_info *btrtl_initialize(struct hci_dev *hdev,
 	u16 hci_rev, lmp_subver;
 	u8 hci_ver, lmp_ver, chip_type = 0;
 	int ret;
-	int rc;
 	u8 key_id;
 	u8 reg_val[2];
 
@@ -1186,8 +1185,8 @@ struct btrtl_device_info *btrtl_initialize(struct hci_dev *hdev,
 		goto err_free;
 	}
 
-	rc = btrtl_vendor_read_reg16(hdev, RTL_SEC_PROJ, reg_val);
-	if (rc < 0)
+	ret = btrtl_vendor_read_reg16(hdev, RTL_SEC_PROJ, reg_val);
+	if (ret < 0)
 		goto err_free;
 
 	key_id = reg_val[0];
